#: src/extensions/snippets.md:3
msgid "Snippets"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:5
msgid "Extensions may provide snippets for one or more languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:7
msgid ""
"Each file containing snippets can be specified in the `snippets` field of "
"the `extensions.toml` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:9
msgid "The referenced path must be relative to the `extension.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:11
msgid "Defining Snippets"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:13
msgid ""
"A given extension may provide one or more snippets. Each snippet must be "
"registered in the `extension.toml`."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:15
msgid ""
"Zed matches snippet files based on the lowercase name of the language (e.g. "
"`rust.json` for Rust). You can use `snippets.json` as a file name to define "
"snippets that will be available regardless of the current buffer language."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:18
msgid ""
"For example, here is an extension that provides snippets for Rust and "
"TypeScript:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:20
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"snippets = [\"./snippets/rust.json\", \"./snippets/typescript.json\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/snippets.md:24
msgid ""
"For more information on how to create snippets, see the [Snippets "
"documentation](../snippets.md)."
msgstr ""
